    {
      "id": "1536033191155081336",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-08-09T15:27:30.888+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "I have a feeling it might be better to have the PCB-side bond pads not be as wide in favor of them being allowed closer; after all, the machien does reliably hit the far smaller passivation openings on the dies....\n\nUnless that means the die would need to be aligned accurately enough to the die ahead of the wire bonding machine getting it's turn; AFAIK that's a premium offer of the factory (alignment by machine to be substantially more precise)",
